--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCOPE / APPROACH
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The web source is an UNROUTED presentational leaf: the automation builder maps a
validation result into `conflicts: AutomationConflict[]` and renders the leaf
inline, which maps each conflict to an `<AlertBanner>` (variant + icon branch on
`severity`: warning → amber/AlertTriangle, else → info/Info), a constant title
`t('automations.builder.conflict','Potential Conflict')`, and a verbatim
`"{automation_name}": {reason}` body — rendering nothing when the list is empty.
Manifest record requires PARITY 3 = 2 states (empty · error) + 1 string
(automations.builder.conflict).

PREDECESSOR REUSE (Honesty Covenant #7 — no predecessor bypass; DRY): the
canonical, fully-stated native surface ALREADY ships as the P4 feature view
TeslaSync/feature-views/ConflictWarnings.{swift,Model,Adapter,Views,Previews,
strings,Tests} (predecessor 0084). It owns the severity→banner projection
(ConflictWarningsProjection → ConflictWarningRow, web icon/title/`"{name}":
{reason}` body), the `ConflictWarningsModel` (@Observable, an S8
`ConflictWarningsSource` seam), and EVERY state — loading skeletons, the
never-a-blank-box empty (web `return null`), the query-error retry, plus the
P4 stale/offline chips. This P7 PAGE unit ships the standalone, deep-linkable
SwiftUI SCREEN that HOSTS that surface unchanged (no second copy) through a
page-level @Observable model + a NavigationDestination seam — exactly mirroring
the accepted sibling page:automations/AutomationCard (Page + PageModel + Route
in Sources/Features/Automations, tests in Tests/Unit/Features/Automations).

OUTPUT-PATH DEVIATION (recorded — no silent drift): the generated prompt names
apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Automations/** (a path that does not exist in this
repo, and which the XcodeGen project.yml does NOT enumerate as a source root, so
files placed there would never compile/test). The real, build-enumerated
conventions are Sources/Features/<Domain>/** (pages) + Tests/Unit/Features/
<Domain>/** (co-located XCTest) + TeslaSync/feature-views/** (the reused
component) — the same roots the sibling P7 automations pages used and were
accepted under. Files shipped there; all compile into the single TeslaSync module.

