--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
IMPLEMENTATION (SwiftUI + Apple HIG)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Navigation entry: ConflictWarningsRouteRegistration.swift exposes the unrouted
  unit as a typed NavigationDestination (ConflictWarningsLink + View
  .conflictWarningsDestination()) any NavigationStack/NavigationSplitView can
  deep-link, plus ConflictWarningsRouteRegistration.make(source:) for a
  ready-built screen over a custom conflict source (no top-level AppRoute claimed
  — the builder owns the inline placement).
- Screen scaffold: ConflictWarningsPage (SwiftUI View) + @Observable @MainActor
  ConflictWarningsPageModel, which owns the reused ConflictWarningsModel
  (`surface`) built over an injectable ConflictWarningsSource (default = two
  representative local conflicts) and exposes load()/refresh(); no business logic
  in the view body; no networking (ADR-004). The page renders
  ConflictWarnings(model: model.surface) inside an adaptive scaffold.
- Adaptive (ADR-002/006): compact iPhone fills width; macOS/iPad cap the banner
  column to a readable measure (horizontalSizeClass; #if os gated).
- 3 data states: the hosted surface drives loading (skeletons) / empty
  (ContentUnavailableView, web `return null`) / error (message + Retry) /
  conflicts(list); the manifest's required `empty` + `error` render from the
  bound @Observable surface. Never a blank region (ADR-013).
- Live/freshness (ADR-013): the surface's stale + offline chips downgrade the
  conflict-check freshness; the page model passes those flags through.
- i18n (ADR-014): page nav title via the catalog key automations.conflicts.title;
  the hosted banner title resolves automations.builder.conflict; web key names
  preserved verbatim. No hardcoded literals.
- a11y (ADR-015): the reused banner sets VoiceOver labels
  (ConflictWarningsAccessibility.bannerSummary = title + severity word + body);
  Dynamic Type; light/dark; the scaffold's teslaSyncTheme().
- Units (ADR-005): N/A — no SI quantities on this surface.

